        {
          "id": "60f57fc1d967551ad64e8c76",
          "questionNumber": 1,
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p><strong>Fill in the blank with the correct option</strong></p>\n\n<p>The teacher asked the student if the homework she ______&nbsp;got completed. otherwise, she will call their parents for a meeting.</p>",
          "image": null,
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "label": "1",
              "text": "had given",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "label": "2",
              "text": "gave",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "3",
              "label": "3",
              "text": "is given",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "4",
              "label": "4",
              "text": "was given",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "5",
              "label": "5",
              "text": "is giving",
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctOptionId": "1",
          "marks": 0.5,
          "negativeMarks": 0.125,
          "explanation": "<p>The correct answer is<strong>&nbsp;option 1 i.e. had given.</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Key Points</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>If a<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">&nbsp;principal clause</span>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">past&nbsp;</span>tense then the&nbsp;<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">dependent&nbsp;</span>clause will also be in the&nbsp;<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">past&nbsp;</span>tense.</li>\n\t<li>The above sentence is in the past tense, thus the dependent clause will be in<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">&nbsp;past perfect.</span></li>\n\t<li>The structure of&nbsp;<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">past perfect tense is- sub + had +V3 (past participle) + object.</span></li>\n\t<li>In the above sentence, the homework is already given&nbsp;that&nbsp;the teacher&nbsp;is asking the student.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Correct answer -&nbsp;</strong><em>The teacher asked the student if the homework&nbsp;she<strong> had given </strong>got completed.</em>&nbsp;otherwise, she will call their parents for a meeting.<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-a0631bfa-7fff-74c5-d42b-e6a6919833f5\"><span style=\"  background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"><span style=\"border:none;display:inline-block;overflow:hidden;width:20px;height:20px;\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/NrgPjv3pok5EMtHAQUkp1j280dIK8nFlSQOuqf4-x5sZt8BoPjKewQTh3fxMHLX5WaVyJp99lUPZHdzzMCwxS9b2qmQHatpk8HOjCii947xJo-vFeSAPNJu6-LHK57kuNcHwGwuY\" style=\"margin-left:0px;margin-top:0px;\" width=\"20\" /></span></span><span style=\"  background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;\"> </span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Simple past tense is used when the subject is narrating about recent past</span></li>\n\t<li><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Perfect past tense is used when Subject is narrating about the thing which has not happened in the recent past.</span></li>\n</ul>",
          "topic": "Test"
        },
        {
          "id": "60f56c0fb464bb9e10ae4956",
          "questionNumber": 2,
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p><strong>Fill in the blanks with Correct Option</strong></p>\n\n<p>They ______ to collect funds for their new startup which is being planned and enacted with the help of various financial advisers.</p>",
          "image": null,
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "label": "1",
              "text": "has began",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "label": "2",
              "text": "have began",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "3",
              "label": "3",
              "text": "has begun",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "4",
              "label": "4",
              "text": "have begun",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "5",
              "label": "5",
              "text": "is began",
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctOptionId": "4",
          "marks": 0.5,
          "negativeMarks": 0.125,
          "explanation": "<p>The correct answer is o<strong>ption 4 i.e. have begun.</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Key Points</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>The&nbsp;third form of the verb&nbsp;is used with&nbsp;<strong>has/have.</strong></li>\n\t<li>has&nbsp;is used for the&nbsp;singular&nbsp;subject while&nbsp;<strong>have&nbsp;</strong>is used for the&nbsp;plural&nbsp;subject.</li>\n\t<li><strong>Begun</strong>&nbsp;is the third form of&nbsp;Begin. It is&nbsp;used in the&nbsp;<strong>present perfect tense</strong>&nbsp;with the helping verb <strong>has/have.</strong></li>\n\t<li>In the above sentence, the start-up is planned, and the subject has started collecting&nbsp;the funds&nbsp;in the past and is continuing it.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p><strong>Correct&nbsp;sentence</strong>-&nbsp;<em>They&nbsp;<strong>have begun</strong> to collect funds for their new start-up which is being planned&nbsp;</em>and enacted with the help of various financial advisers<em>.</em></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><strong>First</strong> verb form - Begin</li>\n\t<li><strong>second</strong> verb Form - Began</li>\n\t<li><strong>Third </strong>Verb From - Begun</li>\n</ul>",
          "topic": "Test"
        },
        {
          "id": "606998182405a57c9f898f89",
          "questionNumber": 3,
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Direction: Pick out the most appropriate word from the words given below each sentence to complete it meaningfully.</span></p>\n\n<p>I read an ______ book.</p>",
          "image": null,
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "label": "1",
              "text": "interested",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "label": "2",
              "text": "interests",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "3",
              "label": "3",
              "text": "interesting",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "4",
              "label": "4",
              "text": "interest",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "5",
              "label": "5",
              "text": "none of these",
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctOptionId": "3",
          "marks": 0.5,
          "negativeMarks": 0.125,
          "explanation": "<p>The correct answer is&nbsp;<strong>interesting</strong>.</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Key Points</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<p>The explanation is as follows:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>The word book is a<strong>&nbsp;noun.</strong></li>\n\t<li>The word preceding the noun is usually&nbsp;<strong>an adjective.</strong></li>\n\t<li>Adjectives are sometimes formed using<strong>&nbsp;\"-ing\".</strong></li>\n\t<li>Hence, the third option is an&nbsp;<strong>adjective.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Hence, the&nbsp;<strong>correct sentence</strong>&nbsp;is<em>&nbsp;I read an<strong>&nbsp;interesting</strong>&nbsp;book.</em></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<p>List of Adjectives ending in&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>&#39;-ING&#39;</strong>.</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Alarmed - Alarming.</li>\n\t<li>Aggravated - Aggravating.</li>\n\t<li>Amused - Amusing.</li>\n\t<li>Annoyed - Annoying.</li>\n\t<li>Astonished - Astonishing.</li>\n\t<li>Astounded - Astounding.</li>\n\t<li>Bored - Boring.</li>\n\t<li>Captivated - Captivating.</li>\n</ul>",
          "topic": "Test"
        },
