          ],
          "correctOptionId": "1",
          "marks": 0.5,
          "negativeMarks": 0.125,
          "explanation": "<div>\n<p>The correct answer is<strong>&nbsp;interviewing.</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Key Points</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<p>The explanation is as follows:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>The word&nbsp;<strong>&#39;in&#39;</strong>&nbsp;is a preposition.</li>\n\t<li>Generally, the &#39;<strong>-ing&#39;&nbsp;</strong>form is used after a<strong>&nbsp;preposition.&nbsp;</strong></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Hence, the&nbsp;<strong>correct sentence</strong>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<em>Her experience in&nbsp;<strong>interviewing</strong>&nbsp;will be beneficial.</em></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Prepositions:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>A preposition usually precedes&nbsp;<strong>a noun or a pronoun.</strong></li>\n\t<li>Some commonly used&nbsp;<strong>prepositions</strong>&nbsp;are:\n\t<ul>\n\t\t<li>above, across, against, along, among, around, at, etc.</li>\n\t\t<li>before, behind, below, beneath, beside, between, by, etc.</li>\n\t\t<li>down, from, in, into, near, of, off, on, to, etc.</li>\n\t\t<li>toward, under, upon, with, and within, etc.</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n</div>",
          "topic": "Test"
        },
