        {
          "id": "606999191ad8005de96a1d46",
          "questionNumber": 6,
          "type": "mcq",
          "text": "<p><strong>Direction: Pick out the most appropriate word from the words given below each sentence to complete it meaningfully.</strong></p>\n\n<p>The pencils ________ on the desk belong to the professor.</p>",
          "image": null,
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "label": "1",
              "text": "sat",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "label": "2",
              "text": "sit",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "3",
              "label": "3",
              "text": "sitting&nbsp;",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "4",
              "label": "4",
              "text": "sits",
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "5",
              "label": "5",
              "text": "none of these",
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctOptionId": "3",
          "marks": 0.5,
          "negativeMarks": 0.125,
          "explanation": "<div>The correct answer is&nbsp;<strong>sitting.</strong></div>\n\n<div><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Key Points</u></span></strong></span></div>\n\n<div>The explanation is as follows:</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>The given sentence is a <strong>reduced relative clause</strong> of&nbsp;<em>The pencils that are sitting on the desk belong to the professor.</em></li>\n\t<li>The verb in &#39;-ing&#39;&nbsp;form is sometimes used to include additional information in a sentence in a reduced relative clause.&nbsp;</li>\n\t<li>The third option is of the<strong> &#39;-ing&#39;&nbsp;</strong>form.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div>Hence, the&nbsp;<span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">correct sentence</span>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<em>The pencils <strong>sitting</strong></em>&nbsp;<em>on the desk belong&nbsp;to the professor.&nbsp;</em></div>\n\n<div><span style=\"display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;\"><img height=\"26px\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png\" width=\"26px\" /><strong><span style=\"vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;\"><u>Additional Information</u></span></strong></span>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>Let us understand reduced relative clause:</div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Reduced relative clauses refer to the<strong> shortening of a relative clause.</strong></li>\n\t<li>This relative clause <strong>modifies the subject </strong>of the&nbsp;sentence.</li>\n\t<li>Reduced relative clauses do not modify&nbsp;the object of a sentence.</li>\n\t<li>Relative clauses are also known as <strong>adjective clauses</strong> as they&nbsp;modify nouns.</li>\n</ul>",
          "topic": "Test"
        },
